{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773765928,"nonce":"f2UHkLCTSvmgkBg+u3PxpaxOHW8=","title":"Detect auth failures instead of burning through max resumes","message":"When the Claude API token expires, the agent fails at step 0. SessionRunner burns through MAX_RESUMES (10) retrying with the same bad token. By the time the user refreshes the token, the session is dead.\n\nThe system should detect auth failures, set a distinct status (suspended:auth-failure), notify the user, and have the watcher retry on a slow interval since the fix is external.\n\nREQ-002, REQ-004","files":null}]}